  "definition": "An orbital element is one value in a parameter set used to describe an orbit. For an ideal two-body trajectory, six independent quantities fix the orbit's size and shape, the orientation of its plane, the direction of periapsis and the body's position along the orbit at an epoch. Element sets are compact and useful for analysis, but their meaning depends on conventions that must accompany the six numbers.[^1][^2]",
